# AI-Powered Excel Analysis Agent

## What it does & the problem it solves
Many students and small business owners in Pakistan collect data in Excel but don't have the
statistical skills to understand it. This AI agent takes any Excel spreadsheet, automatically
computes real statistics and detects data anomalies using machine learning, then uses an AI
agent to explain the findings in plain English — key insights, data quality issues, and
recommended actions.

**Who it's for:** students, freelancers, and small business owners who use Excel but lack data
analysis skills.

## Live URL
  [Live App](https://excel-insights--erajfatima14.replit.app/api/docs)

Open the link above — it's FastAPI's interactive documentation page. No login required.
Try `POST /api/analyze` (upload an Excel file) or `GET /api/healthz` to test it directly.

## Features
- Upload any .xlsx or .xls file for instant analysis
- Automatic statistics: row/column counts, missing values, mean/median/std per column
- Machine learning-based anomaly detection (Isolation Forest)
- AI agent that turns statistics into plain-English insights and recommendations
- Clean error handling for invalid files and API failures

## The AI feature
After computing statistics and running anomaly detection, the results are sent to an LLM
(Groq API, Llama 3.3 70B) with this system prompt, written by me:

You are a senior data analyst. You will be given statistics computed from an uploaded Excel
spreadsheet: row/column counts, missing value percentages per column, basic statistics (mean,
median, std) for numeric columns, and a list of anomalous rows detected by an Isolation Forest
model. Based on this information, respond with ONLY a valid JSON object containing: a
plain-English summary, key insights, data quality issues, and recommended actions. Be specific
and reference actual column names and numbers from the statistics given to you.

The AI never sees the raw spreadsheet data itself — only the computed statistics — which keeps
the analysis fast and privacy-conscious.

## Tools, services, and models used
- Python, FastAPI
- pandas, scikit-learn (Isolation Forest for anomaly detection)
- Groq API (Llama 3.3 70B)
- Deployed on Replit

